--- !u!114 &624205745
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 624205739}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8cdd1c6f6203178409de95432885bc10, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _indicator: {fileID: 941887225}
  Dialogue:
  - In the middle of all this, Bragi, the narrator, does not wish for this world
    to end. He is torn; he loves the story as it is laid out for him, a tragic tale
    of a child struggling to find their identity while freeing their father from
    the tyranny and torture of the All-Father, but he knows that if he lets the story
    reach its conclusion he, alongside the rest of the worlds, will die, so he has
    to fight you.
  - "The Lie is given the choice to walk away, left unsatisfied and unable to complete
    their purpose, but now given the ability to live their own life. Roll credits.
    Alternatively, they have to fight their way through Bragi to free Loki. Bragi
    acts as the final boss of the game. Should you defeat him, the Lie may free their
    father and unite with him and Sigyn. They have completed their purpose, but at
    the cost of Ragnar\xF6k being set in motion."
